fety  reasons this former site lies still and  unused a huge failure says the boss in  energy policy and planning even if you  were fracking for british gas that  wouldn't affect the price would it  because you'd still sell it at market  price it may well affect the price we've  got to be able to do it more cheaply  than taking shale gas from the united  states putting it on a boat sailing  across the atlantic you know people are  saying well that will make a difference  because it doesn't affect prices  tomorrow well the reason we're in this  mess is because we haven't thought about  this  you know 10 years ago the only real  shield is alternative sources nuclear  solar or wind  but all are still too fledgling to cover  demand  energy security is not just about supply  it's about supply that's affordable if  russia turned off the taps we'd still be  able to turn on the lights but at what  cost and for how long  helen ann smith sky news in great  yarmouth
 

